        "# virtual subclass\n",
        "\n",
        "A class recognized as a subclass of an abstract base class without inheriting from it, for example by registration with `ABC.register`. It does not inherit the ABC's methods.\n",
        "\n",
        "[Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-virtual-subclass)"
      ]
    }
